  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as both a noun and a suru verb. Covers a range of contexts: showing ID or tickets, presenting evidence, offering terms or proposals. The act implies deliberately putting something forward for another person to see or consider. More formal than {見|み}せる (to show).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {身分証|みぶんしょう}を{提示|ていじ}する: to present identification\n- {条件|じょうけん}を{提示|ていじ}する: to present conditions\n- {証拠|しょうこ}を{提示|ていじ}する: to present evidence\n- {価格|かかく}を{提示|ていじ}する: to quote a price\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {提出|ていしゅつ}: submission (handing over documents formally)\n- {掲示|けいじ}: posting, notice (displaying for public view)\n- {表示|ひょうじ}: display, indication (on screens or labels)",
